# kdwire.obligations -- disposition for every `allium plan` obligation of kdwire.allium.
# Gate: host-lifecycle obligations specs/kdwire.allium --tests tests --strict-discharge
#   <id> => test:<name> [exercises=<symbol>] | structural | waived: <reason>
# `structural` is only ever a declared shape: field presence and types, an optional
# field's two cases, a declared terminal or rejected transition, a surface's actor.
# Nothing behavioural is dispositioned structural, because the check lane does not
# discharge behaviour and a relabel is the dodge this gate exists to catch.
#
# The law names, and where each is measured. THE ID LAW is the pair
# `IssueOnTheExpectedId` and `FlipOnlyOnAnAcceptedId`, and the flip is asserted in both directions:
# an acknowledgement of the id last issued moves the pair, one of any other id does not. THE PARITY
# LAW is one invariant over every reply, discharged wherever a reply is built. THE DRAIN-ACK LAW is
# discharged by the hold, which answers an awaited packet while the machine is frozen. THE BACKLOG
# FLUSH is the count of stale chunks the hold-entry log records.

entity-fields.ByteArray                                  => structural
entity-fields.Endpoint                                   => structural
